1255
00:55:13.740 --> 00:55:15.000
A room with a view.
真是个有风景的房间。

1256
00:55:15.220 --> 00:55:17.780
And it was like a just a freight train.
感觉就像是一列货运列车。

1257
00:55:17.880 --> 00:55:19.280
There was not a passenger train.
那不是客运列车。

1258
00:55:19.580 --> 00:55:27.220
You know what I love about this is that the view from the writers rooms was actually like woven into this episode.
你知道我最喜欢这个地方的是什么吗？编剧办公室的视野实际上被巧妙地编织进了这一集里。

1259
00:55:27.220 --> 00:55:28.700
And I just kind of love that.
我真的挺喜欢这样的。

1260
00:55:28.700 --> 00:55:38.340
But I used to say that if we were ever confronted with an actual zombie apocalypse in real life while working on the office,
但我以前常说，如果在我们制作《办公室》期间，现实生活中真的遭遇了僵尸末日，

1261
00:55:38.560 --> 00:55:45.540
we'd be in a great position because we could head over to the gunnery, arm ourselves and then hop the train.
我们处境会非常棒，因为我们可以直接去火器铺武装自己，然后跳上火车。

1262
00:55:45.540 --> 00:55:55.160
And yes, it just felt like, you know, a good spot to be in should zombies suddenly overrun the world.
而且没错，这就感觉像是，你知道的，万一僵尸突然占领了全世界，那会是个不错的好地方。

1263
00:55:55.680 --> 00:56:01.160
Listen, I know there's no zombies in it, but I'm pretty sure John Wick would agree he'd have his gunnery.
听着，我知道里面没有僵尸，但我很确定约翰·威克会同意的，他会有他的武器库。

1264
00:56:01.160 --> 00:56:02.780
He'd have some transportation.
他会有些交通工具。

1265
00:56:03.540 --> 00:56:07.660
Jenna, I finally watched all the John Wick movies like you told me to.
珍娜，我终于把所有的《疾速追杀》电影都看完了，就像你跟我说的那样。

1266
00:56:08.500 --> 00:56:09.920
You watched all of them?
你把它们全都看了？

1267
00:56:10.440 --> 00:56:11.440
What are you talking about?
你在说什么呢？

1268
00:56:11.640 --> 00:56:12.780
You told me to go watch them all.
你叫我去把它们全看完的。

1269
00:56:12.880 --> 00:56:14.580
You said you have to see the John Wick movies.
你说你必须看看《疾速追杀》系列电影。

1270
00:56:14.780 --> 00:56:15.940
What are you talking about?
你在说什么啊？

1271
00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:17.600
What are you talking about?
你在说什么呀？

1272
00:56:18.280 --> 00:56:21.140
I said watch Keanu Reeves movies.
我说的是看基努·里维斯的电影。

1273
00:56:21.560 --> 00:56:23.480
Like, no, you told me.
不对，你告诉过我。

1274
00:56:23.660 --> 00:56:26.160
Like Speed and the Matrix.
比如《生死时速》和《黑客帝国》。

1275
00:56:26.860 --> 00:56:27.460
Hold up, lady.
等一下，大姐。

1276
00:56:27.680 --> 00:56:29.520
You told me to watch the John Wick movie.
你叫我去看《疾速追杀》电影的。

1277
00:56:29.820 --> 00:56:31.680
You said you, Sam, Sam.
你说过，山姆，山姆。

1278
00:56:32.320 --> 00:56:32.900
No, I.
不，我。

1279
00:56:33.120 --> 00:56:33.640
Sam.
山姆。

1280
00:56:34.220 --> 00:56:34.740
Guys.
伙计们。

1281
00:56:35.200 --> 00:56:38.600
For taking this to court, you did very excitedly.
为了把这事闹上法庭，你表现得非常兴奋。

1282
00:56:38.880 --> 00:56:40.760
This has come up multiple times.
这已经提做好多次了。

1283
00:56:41.080 --> 00:56:42.740
You told me to watch John Wick.
你叫我去看《疾速追杀》的。

1284
00:56:42.740 --> 00:56:45.040
How good the movies are, how attractive he is in the movies.
说电影有多么好看，他在电影里有多么有吸引力。

1285
00:56:45.240 --> 00:56:46.780
Lady, how many are there?
大姐，总共有几部啊？

1286
00:56:47.500 --> 00:56:48.380
There are three.
有三部。

1287
00:56:48.700 --> 00:56:50.560
I did a marathon of them.
我一口气马拉松式地把它们全看完了。

1288
00:56:50.900 --> 00:56:52.280
Okay, here's the thing.
好吧，情况是这样的。

1289
00:56:52.420 --> 00:56:57.780
I spoke passionately about my love of Keanu Reeves movies, how they were getting me through
我满腔热情地表达了我对基努·里维斯电影的喜爱，它们是如何陪我度过

1290
00:56:57.780 --> 00:56:58.520
the pandemic.
疫情的。

1291
00:56:58.860 --> 00:57:05.960
I watched the first half of the first John Wick movie, but we couldn't finish it all
我看了第一部《疾速追杀》的前半部分，但我们没能在

1292
00:57:05.960 --> 00:57:06.500
in one night.
一个晚上看完。

1293
00:57:06.600 --> 00:57:08.020
Now, listen, I loved it.
听着，我很喜欢它。

1294
00:57:08.240 --> 00:57:09.940
Look at my face right now.
看看我现在这表情。

1295
00:57:10.080 --> 00:57:11.540
I loved the coins.
我很喜欢那些金币。

1296
00:57:11.540 --> 00:57:16.060
I loved how he had his coffee cups on a little towel next to his coffee machine, and Lee
我很喜欢他把咖啡杯放在咖啡机旁的一条小毛巾上，李

1297
00:57:16.060 --> 00:57:20.540
and I started doing that because we were inspired by what we saw in the John Wick movie, but
和我开始这样做，因为我们受到了《疾速追杀》电影中看到的启发，但是

1298
00:57:20.540 --> 00:57:21.760
we didn't finish it.
我们没有把它看完。

1299
00:57:22.140 --> 00:57:22.860
Shut the front door.
我的天哪。

1300
00:57:22.860 --> 00:57:25.580
Because, you know, we rented it, and then the rental ran out.
因为，你知道的，我们租了它，然后租期到了。

1301
00:57:25.800 --> 00:57:26.820
Shut the front door.
少来这套。

1302
00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:28.920
You gave me this whole call to action.
你刚才跟我扯了半天行动号召。

1303
00:57:29.240 --> 00:57:35.600
Which, by the way, now that I know you haven't even finished the first one, now it makes sense
顺便说一句，现在我才知道你连第一部都没看完，我总算明白了

1304
00:57:35.600 --> 00:57:39.720
to me why you went on and on about that towel by his coffee mug, because you never see that
为什么你之前滔滔不绝地谈论他咖啡杯旁边的毛巾，因为你根本再也

1305
00:57:39.720 --> 00:57:40.080
again.
看不到那条毛巾了。

1306
00:57:40.280 --> 00:57:45.940
That's like five seconds, and then it's nothing but ass-kicking for three movies.
那大概也就五秒钟，然后接下来的三部电影就全都是打打杀杀。

1307
00:57:46.180 --> 00:57:48.660
Listen, there's no more coffee mug.
听着，后面没有咖啡杯了。

1308
00:57:48.760 --> 00:57:49.960
His whole house burns down.
他整栋房子都被烧毁了。

1309
00:57:51.480 --> 00:57:53.460
They blow his f***ing house up.
他们把他那该死的房子给炸了。

1310
00:57:55.650 --> 00:57:57.090
Now it makes sense to me.
现在我可算明白了。

1311
00:57:57.090 --> 00:57:58.690
And I said, I watched it with Josh.
我说过，我和乔什一起看的。

1312
00:57:58.830 --> 00:58:00.670
I was like, Josh, we have to watch John Wick.
当时我说，乔什，我们得看看《疾速追杀》。

1313
00:58:00.830 --> 00:58:01.930
Jenna said, we have to watch it.
珍娜说，我们必须得看。

1314
00:58:02.050 --> 00:58:05.330
And then I'm looking for the coffee pot, and I'm like, why is she talking so much about
然后我在找咖啡壶，我就想，她怎么一直在喋喋不休地谈论

1315
00:58:05.330 --> 00:58:05.970
this coffee pot?
这个咖啡壶？

1316
00:58:06.130 --> 00:58:06.970
Now it makes sense.
现在我懂了。

1317
00:58:07.030 --> 00:58:08.890
You've only seen like 20 minutes of the movie.
你大概只看了二十分钟的电影。

1318
00:58:09.090 --> 00:58:10.690
I saw the whole first half.
我看了整整前半部。

1319
00:58:10.850 --> 00:58:11.870
Here's where I ended.
我看到这里停下的。

1320
00:58:12.050 --> 00:58:17.410
He's been really injured after a big fight at that weird club where all the, you know,
他在那个奇怪的夜总会经历了一场大战后受了重伤，所有那些，你知道的，

1321
00:58:17.530 --> 00:58:18.150
assassins-
杀手——

1322
00:58:18.150 --> 00:58:18.790
Yes, he goes.
对，他去了。

1323
00:58:18.990 --> 00:58:20.370
Constantly goes to a rave.
经常去狂欢派对。

1324
00:58:20.610 --> 00:58:23.350
A gazillion assassins always are at a rave.
无数的杀手总是在狂欢派对上。

1325
00:58:23.350 --> 00:58:28.090
Yes, and he gets really wounded, and then that doctor like shoots him up with adrenaline,
对，他受了重伤，然后那个医生给他注射了肾上腺素，

1326
00:58:28.090 --> 00:58:33.750
and he should definitely be resting, and he's about to go out and do more ass-kicking,
他本来绝对应该好好休息的，结果他马上又要出去大开杀戒了，

1327
00:58:33.790 --> 00:58:36.950
and I was tired, and I was worried for him.
我很累，而且我很替他担心。

1328
00:58:37.250 --> 00:58:41.430
You know, I told you I don't like it when people who have injuries continue to injure themselves.
你知道的，我跟你说过，我不喜欢看那些身负重伤的人继续折腾自己。

1329
00:58:41.450 --> 00:58:41.750
What?
什么？

1330
00:58:41.890 --> 00:58:42.970
I needed a break.
我需要休息一下。

1331
00:58:43.290 --> 00:58:47.750
Well, then you might as well not watch the rest, because he literally gets stitched up,
好吧，那你干脆别看剩下的了，因为他 literalmente（字面意思上）伤口刚缝好，

1332
00:58:47.830 --> 00:58:49.370
and then people punch him in his stitches.
然后就有人往他的伤口上打拳。

1333
00:58:49.590 --> 00:58:49.770
No!
不会吧！

1334
00:58:49.770 --> 00:58:51.950
And also, he is running.
而且，他还在奔跑。

1335
00:58:51.950 --> 00:58:55.230
He is limping through, like, Rome or somewhere.
他一瘸一拐地穿过罗马或者什么地方。

1336
00:58:55.530 --> 00:58:55.990
Rome?
罗马？

1337
00:58:56.230 --> 00:58:57.490
How does he get to Rome?
他怎么去罗马了？

1338
00:58:57.670 --> 00:58:58.590
Second movie, second movie.
第二部，第二部里去的。

1339
00:58:58.730 --> 00:59:02.590
And I literally turned to Josh, and I said, you know what I can't handle right now?
我当时真的转头对乔什说，你知道我现在最受不了什么吗？

1340
00:59:02.630 --> 00:59:04.650
Is if he gets hit by another car.
就是他又被车撞。

1341
00:59:04.950 --> 00:59:11.910
And literally, three seconds after I said that, a car runs over him and sends him flying in the air.
说来也巧，就在我说完三秒钟后，一辆车从他身上碾过去，把他撞飞到了空中。

1342
00:59:12.530 --> 00:59:18.530
Sorry, that was a really long tangent for us guys, but mouth agape?
抱歉，刚才我们扯得有点远了，不过当时我目瞪口呆？

1343
00:59:18.710 --> 00:59:20.670
I am now the John Wick expert?
我现在成《疾速追杀》专家了？

1344
00:59:20.670 --> 00:59:22.150
How the hell did that happen?
这到底是怎么回事？

1345
00:59:22.750 --> 00:59:24.610
Well, I feel like I should watch them.
好吧，我觉得我应该把它们看完。

1346
00:59:24.830 --> 00:59:26.290
Well, I think you should.
嗯，我觉得你应该看。

1347
00:59:26.470 --> 00:59:27.490
I think I will.
我想我会看的。

1348
00:59:27.750 --> 00:59:30.970
But get ready, because there's a lot of wound on wound.
不过做好心理准备，因为里面有很多伤上加伤。

1349
00:59:31.250 --> 00:59:33.310
I don't like seeing wound on wound.
我可不喜欢看伤上加伤的画面。

1350
00:59:33.370 --> 00:59:33.590
Well.
好吧。

1351
00:59:33.790 --> 00:59:34.790
It's hard for me.
这对我来说很难。

1352
00:59:35.470 --> 00:59:35.990
Okay.
好吧。

1353
00:59:35.990 --> 00:59:36.890
I don't know.
我不知道。

1354
00:59:37.010 --> 00:59:37.830
Where are we?
我们到哪了？

1355
00:59:38.030 --> 00:59:39.150
Well, here we are.
好吧，我们到了。

1356
00:59:39.630 --> 00:59:41.590
Angela walks over to Andy.
安吉拉向安迪走去。

1357
00:59:41.590 --> 00:59:43.690
Andy, she's holding the crazy cat.
安迪，她抱着那只疯猫。

1358
00:59:43.830 --> 00:59:46.910
And she says, you may ask me out to dinner.
她说，你可以约我吃晚饭。

1359
00:59:47.250 --> 00:59:47.770
Yes.
好的。

1360
00:59:47.890 --> 00:59:53.290
She says, nothing fancy or foreign, no bars, no patios, no vegetables, and no seafood.
她说，不要太花哨，不要外国菜，不要酒吧，不要露台，不要蔬菜，也不要海鲜。

1361
00:59:53.650 --> 00:59:55.050
What's up with no vegetables?
不吃蔬菜是怎么回事？

1362
00:59:55.430 --> 00:59:55.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

1363
00:59:55.810 --> 00:59:56.610
She's a vegetarian.
她是素食主义者。

1364
00:59:56.910 --> 00:59:57.950
What does she eat?
那她吃什么？

1365
00:59:58.250 --> 01:00:00.770
Are you going to eat, what, rice, pasta?
你打算吃什么，米饭，面条？

1366
01:00:00.770 --> 01:00:01.790
What will you eat?
你会吃什么？

1367
01:00:01.890 --> 01:00:03.550
My cauliflower spaghetti.
我的花椰菜意面。

1368
01:00:03.910 --> 01:00:04.930
That's a vegetable.
那可是蔬菜。

1369
01:00:05.270 --> 01:00:05.770
I know.
我知道。

1370
01:00:05.770 --> 01:00:07.050
Cauliflower spaghetti.
花椰菜意面。

1371
01:00:07.050 --> 01:00:08.110
Hold the cauliflower.
不加花椰菜。

1372
01:00:08.550 --> 01:00:11.290
She's not going to make it easy on Andy, for sure.
她肯定不会让安迪好过。

1373
01:00:11.830 --> 01:00:13.490
Well, Dwight is crushed.
德怀特心碎了。

1374
01:00:13.530 --> 01:00:15.430
He runs to his stairwell.
他跑进楼梯间。

1375
01:00:15.690 --> 01:00:21.910
This is where he goes to pump himself up, or maybe where he goes to deal with sad feelings.
这是他给自己打气的地方，也许也是他处理悲伤情绪的地方。

1376
01:00:21.910 --> 01:00:24.590
This is his, I guess, little spot.
这是他的，我猜，小地方。

1377
01:00:24.930 --> 01:00:26.730
This is his emotional nook.
这是他的情感角落。

1378
01:00:27.090 --> 01:00:27.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1379
01:00:27.790 --> 01:00:29.670
And Jim follows him.
然后吉姆跟了过去。

1380
01:00:29.790 --> 01:00:31.270
He tries to comfort him.
他试图安慰他。

1381
01:00:31.270 --> 01:00:36.630
And it's really sweet, because he kind of talks about his relationship with Pam and
这真的很温馨，因为他谈到了他与帕姆的关系以及

1382
01:00:36.630 --> 01:00:37.670
his own heartbreak.
他自己的心碎经历。

1383
01:00:38.070 --> 01:00:40.370
Listen, you know, I watched this episode three times.
听着，你知道，我看了这集三遍。

1384
01:00:40.870 --> 01:00:44.410
And the first time I watched it, I was like, oh, that's so sweet of Jim.
我第一次看的时候，心想，哦，吉姆太暖心了。

1385
01:00:44.630 --> 01:00:46.350
He's giving Dwight a pep talk.
他在给德怀特打气。

1386
01:00:46.670 --> 01:00:46.870
Okay.
好吧。

1387
01:00:47.170 --> 01:00:52.510
By the third time I watched it, I was like, some flippin' pep talk.
等我看到第三遍的时候，心想，这算哪门子打气啊。

1388
01:00:52.850 --> 01:00:56.210
I mean, this would, like, depress the hell out of me.
我的意思是，这简直能把我郁闷死。

1389
01:00:56.470 --> 01:00:58.630
Like, is this the speech you say?
话说，这是你说的话吗？

1390
01:00:58.630 --> 01:00:59.710
This is what he said.
他是这么说的。

1391
01:00:59.710 --> 01:01:01.970
I mean, she was with Roy, right?
我的意思是，她以前和罗伊在一起，对吧？

1392
01:01:02.150 --> 01:01:02.890
Talking about Pam.
谈论的是帕姆。

1393
01:01:03.250 --> 01:01:06.250
And then he says, and I quote, I just couldn't take it.
然后他说，原话是，我就是受不了。

1394
01:01:06.390 --> 01:01:07.530
I mean, I lost it, Dwight.
我是说，我崩溃了，德怀特。

1395
01:01:07.650 --> 01:01:08.350
I couldn't sleep.
我睡不着觉。

1396
01:01:08.550 --> 01:01:10.070
I couldn't concentrate on anything.
我什么也集中不了精神。

1397
01:01:10.470 --> 01:01:12.890
Even weird stuff, like food, had no taste.
甚至奇怪的事情，比如食物，都索然无味。

1398
01:01:13.030 --> 01:01:15.230
So my solution was to move away.
所以我的解决方案是搬走。

1399
01:01:15.410 --> 01:01:16.390
It was awful.
太可怕了。

1400
01:01:16.630 --> 01:01:19.810
It was something that I wouldn't wish on my worst enemy.
那种感觉我连对最讨厌的敌人都不希望有。

1401
01:01:20.230 --> 01:01:20.870
Pep talk!
打气鼓劲！

1402
01:01:21.370 --> 01:01:23.510
But Jim and Pam are together now.
可是吉姆和帕姆现在在一起了。

1403
01:01:23.510 --> 01:01:29.290
So is the rest of that scene that he's sort of saying, like, listen, I've been where you
所以那一幕剩下的部分，他其实是在表达，听着，我经历过你

1404
01:01:29.290 --> 01:01:31.110
are, but look where I am now.
现在的处境，但看看我现在。

1405
01:01:31.130 --> 01:01:32.310
It's gonna be okay.
一切都会好起来的。

1406
01:01:32.450 --> 01:01:33.970
He just doesn't say that part.
他只是没说后半部分。

1407
01:01:34.150 --> 01:01:35.570
He doesn't say any of that.
他根本没说那些。

1408
01:01:35.750 --> 01:01:36.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1409
01:01:36.210 --> 01:01:38.970
He literally says, I wouldn't wish it on my worst enemy.
他原话是，我连最恨的仇敌都不希望经历这种事。

1410
01:01:38.970 --> 01:01:40.130
And that includes you.
其中也包括你。

1411
